{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal-record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or require an applicant to disclose a criminal record before making a conditional offer, and after an offer may consider only specified convictions, weighed through an individualized assessment.","key_value":"Conviction lookbacks: 6 years (1st degree), 4 years (2nd/3rd degree), 1 year (4th degree)","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes a dwelling unit in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units. A provider may still consider methamphetamine manufacture or production convictions in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Penalty not to exceed $1,000 with no prior violation in 5 years, $5,000 with one prior in 5 years, $10,000 with two or more priors in 7 years; the director may also order compliance measures, a conditional offer or unit, and up to $1,000 to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer,","interaction":"Does not bar or affect any right or action existing independently, including under P.L.1945, c.169 (C.10:5-1 et seq.).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application-fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting an application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether criminal history is part of its eligibility criteria and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors. The director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes a dwelling unit in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require the applicant’s rental application fee be returned unless housing is provided to the applicant; monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 by violation history.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction of applicant housed by director’s order","requirement":"If a housing provider’s appeal succeeds and the court overturns the director’s order, the provider may evict the former applicant housed in its unit because of that order, with at least 45 days’ notice before the eviction.","key_value":"45 days’ notice","coverage_conditions":"Applies to a former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order under this act, after the provider wins an appeal.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Unit occupied because of the director’s order under the act"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction;","interaction":"Operates notwithstanding any provision of the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
